# Smart Museum Artifact Conservation System

## Operation Schema

| ID | Operation | Precondition | Input | Postcondition |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| OP-01 | Perform Sensor Self-Check | Chamber is powered on. | Sensor status and sensor readings | All essential sensors are verified as working, or failure is detected. |
| OP-02 | Check Environmental-Control Devices | Chamber is powered on and control devices are connected. | Status of temperature, humidity, light and protection controls | Working control devices are identified and available for use. |
| OP-03 | Register Artifact | Artifact is placed inside the chamber. | Artifact ID and identification information | Artifact information is recorded in the system. |
| OP-04 | Load Environmental Profile | Artifact has been registered. | Required temperature, humidity, light and vibration limits | Artifact's environmental requirements are loaded. |
| OP-05 | Monitor Environmental Conditions | Essential sensors are working. | Temperature, humidity, light, vibration, door and power readings | Current environmental conditions are recorded and checked against limits. |
| OP-06 | Check Chamber Door | Door sensor is working. | Door sensor status | System knows whether the chamber door is open or closed. |
| OP-07 | Adjust Temperature | Temperature is outside the permitted range and control is available. | Current temperature and required temperature range | Temperature is adjusted toward the permitted range. |
| OP-08 | Adjust Humidity | Humidity is outside the permitted range and control is available. | Current humidity and required humidity range | Humidity is adjusted toward the permitted range. |
| OP-09 | Verify Environmental Recovery | A temperature or humidity correction has been issued. | New temperature/humidity readings and required limits | System confirms whether the condition has returned to the permitted range. |
| OP-10 | Activate Protection Controls | Environmental condition cannot be corrected within the allowed recovery period. | Environmental failure and artifact condition | Additional protection controls are activated and normal conservation is stopped. |
| OP-11 | Generate Operator Alert | A critical abnormal condition is detected. | Failure details, environmental readings and artifact information | Alert is sent/recorded for the museum operator. |
| OP-12 | Detect Vibration | Artifact is inside and vibration sensor is working. | Vibration level and permitted threshold | Significant vibration is detected and protective action can be triggered. |
| OP-13 | Verify Vibration Stabilization | Significant vibration has previously been detected. | Vibration readings, threshold and stabilization period | System confirms whether vibration has remained below the permitted threshold. |
| OP-14 | Suspend Conservation Activities | Normal conservation is active and a dangerous condition occurs. | Door status, vibration status or critical environmental condition | Normal conservation activities are suspended. |
| OP-15 | Switch to Emergency Power | Normal power has been lost and emergency power is available. | Power failure signal and emergency power status | System switches to emergency power and continues essential protection. |
| OP-16 | Verify Safe Artifact Removal | Artifact is inside and no active protection response is occurring. | Chamber condition, artifact condition, environmental status and protection status | Artifact removal is permitted only when all required safety conditions are satisfied. |
